RL vegans try to limit their use of animal products.  This tends to
include not consuming meat, eggs, milk or gelatin.  For many, this
includes honey.

In addition, RL vegans do not tend to wear leather or wool.

Nethack uses "vegan" to refer to a vegan diet, presumably including 
milk (since candy bars aren't vegan) and honey (neither is royal jelly).

Nethack "vegans" can wear and otherwise use items with animal products.
It would be interesting to divide this conduct up, into "vegan diet" and 
"vegan lifestyle".

With the exception of the use of 7 certain candles[1], vegan lifestyle
would be not using or wearing any animal items.   Armour-wise, this
should be interesting, the best AK kit I can come up with would be the
following -- T-shirt, Dwarvish Mithril, a cloak (MR, probably), any helm
other then elven, only GoP, any shield, kicking boots or iron shoes.  
Nifty little challenge.

Ivory rings could not be worn, nor could candles be used.  Leather drums
and drums of earthquakes are out of the question, so are oilskin
sacks[2].  Oil lamps could not be used, neither could magic lamps or,
probably, brass lanterns (its going to be a dark trip).  Potions of oil
are excluded, and I would exclude "milky" potions as well.  Hope that
leather spellbook wasn't a spell you needed.  Saddles and leashes are
gone as well.  

Whips and slingshots are out of the question, but that shouldn't cause
too much sufferings.  Worm teeth and crysknives should also be excluded, 
IMNSHO.

Unihorns, being bone, is definitely out of the question, and that should
really, really hurt.

So, who wants to code a "vegan lifestyle" patch?  Should be one of the
most annoying conducts out there.

You get to stumble through dark dungeons, in pretty poor gear, no speed
boost from armour, and you better hope that ivory rings and milky
potions aren't items you need.

Have fun.

[1] There is vegan wax, so perhaps only tallow candles would be
excluded...
[2] Would "use" include looting them, or just putting stuff in them...

